      "text": "I have gathered information about *People We Meet on Vacation* and its reception.\n\n### Novel Summary & Themes\n\nThe novel centers on **Poppy and Alex**, best friends who developed a tradition of taking one week-long vacation together every summer for a decade. The story alternates between the **present** (where they are no longer close) and **two years ago** (the trip that caused their rift), tracing the evolution of their friendship into a possible romance. Key themes highlighted include **friendship to romance**, **grief and regret**, **self-discovery**, and the possibility of **second chances**. It utilizes a **dual-timeline** structure and is noted for its witty banter and emotional depth.\n\n*   **Author:** Emily Henry\n*   **Year:** 2021\n*   **Word Count:** Approximately 94,000 words\n\n### Critical Reception and Context\n\nThe novel was **widely reviewed in major outlets** upon its release and has become a key text in its genre. It was **praised for its dual-timeline structure and friendship-to-romance arc**.\n\nIn relation to Emily Henry's other work, critics have drawn **comparisons to her other novels**, suggesting it shares the same celebrated qualities, particularly the complex emotional stakes and witty dialogue found in books like *Beach Read*.\n\nI recommend using the provided Wikipedia and review overview URLs to find specific outlet reviews and detailed Goodreads reception, as I can only provide metadata and summaries here.",
